{% section #install-plugin step=1 title="Install the Appwrite plugin" %}

The fastest way to get started with Appwrite in Codex is to install the **Appwrite plugin** from the official plugin directory. The plugin includes agent skills for the Appwrite CLI and all major SDKs, giving Codex the context it needs to follow the latest Appwrite code patterns.

{% tabs %}
{% tabsitem #desktop title="Desktop app" %}

![Appwrite plugin page in the ChatGPT desktop app](/images/docs/mcp/codex/install-plugin.avif)

- Open the ChatGPT desktop app.
- Click **Plugins** in the sidebar.
- Search for `Appwrite` and select the **Appwrite** plugin.
- Click **Install plugin**.

{% /tabsitem %}
{% tabsitem #cli title="CLI" %}

- Run `codex` in your terminal, then run `/plugins`.
- Switch to the **OpenAI Curated** marketplace.
- Search for `Appwrite` and select the **Appwrite** plugin.
- Select **Install plugin**.

{% /tabsitem %}
{% /tabs %}

Once installed, the language and deployment skills load automatically based on your task. Add the remote Appwrite MCP server in [Step 3](#step-3) so Codex can call Appwrite APIs and search the documentation.

{% info title="Prefer manual setup?" %}

If you'd rather configure the MCP server individually, skip to [Step 3](#step-3).

{% /info %}

{% /section %}

